## 2.6 Cytotoxicity assay
Cytotoxicity was investigated by 3-(4,5-dimethylthiazol-2-yl)-2, 5-diphenyltetrazolium bromide (MTT) (Sigma, USA) assay. For cell viability and half maximal inhibitory concentration \(\left(\mathrm{IC}_{50}\right)\) of \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\), Hela cells, HUVECs or BMSCs were seeded into 96-well plates at a density of \(8\times10^{3}\) cells per well with being cultured for \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\). The cells were treated with \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) at various concentrations for another \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\). Then \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) fresh culture medium and \(10~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) MTT solution were added to each well after the cells were rinsed twice with PBS. After incubation for \(4\,\mathrm{~h~}\) at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\), the absorbance at \(563\;\mathrm{nm}\) was determined using a microplate reader (Thermo, USA). Cytotoxicity curve was based on the absorbance of different groups and \(\mathrm{IC}_{50}\) of \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) were calculated out according to the curve.
## 2.7 Apoptosis assay
Apoptosis of Hela cells was assessed by Annexin V-FITC/PI Cell Apoptosis Kit. Hela cells were seeded into 6-well plates \((15\,\times\,10^{4}\,\mathrm{cells\cdotwell^{-1}})\) and cultured for \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\). Then the plates were added in fresh medium with different \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) concentrations (0, 50, 200, 500, 1,000, \(2,000\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\)). After \(24\,\mathrm{~h~}\) of incubation, the cell apoptosis was detected by Annexin V-FITC/PI Cell Apoptosis Kit using flow cytometry, according to the manufacturer's protocol.
## 2.8 Fluorescence characterization of cell phagocytosis
Hela cells were used to further understand the difference in the effect of micron or nano-sized Mg-MOF74, the loading property of Mg-MOF74 [17] was utilized to adsorb FITC, thereby calibrating the location of MOF during cellular activity. Hela cells were seeded \(2\times10^{4}\) cells \(\mathrm{well}^{-1}\) in a 24-well plate. After \(24\,\mathrm{~h~}\), FITC-Mg-MOF74 (micro or nano) was added in different wells to obtain a \(200\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) culture system in darkness for \(4\,\mathrm{~h~}\), respectively. Then the samples were cleaned, fixed, permeabilized followed by PBS washing and were stained with rhodamine-phalloidin and DAPI. The final images were taken by a fluorescence microscope (Leica, Germany).
