## 2.9 Ion release detection
The concentration of magnesium ions released from the Mg-MOF74 was determined by inductively coupled plasma atomic emission spectrometry (ICP-AES; IRIS Advantage, Thermo Scientific). The \(5\,\mathrm{~mg~}\) Mg-MOF74 specimens were soaked in \(5\,\mathrm{mL}\) of deionized water for 1, 4, 8, 12, and \(24\,\mathrm{~h~}\), respectively, at \(310\,\mathrm{~K~}\) without agitation, and the supernatant was collected and diluted after centrifugation at each time-point. Then every sample was filtrated through \(220\,\upmu\mathrm{m}\) pore size and collected.
## 2.10 Alkaline phosphatase color development and activity assay
The osteogenic basic medium was supplemented with 10 mmol \(\upbeta\)-glycerol phosphate, \(0.2\,\mathrm{~mmol}\) ascorbic acid and \(50\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) vitamin C. Micron and nanoscale Mg-MOF74 were added to the basic osteogenic medium to obtain different concentrations of the target culture solutions (0, 50, 100, 200, \(500\ \upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\)). Osteogenic activities were studied in vitro after 7 days of cell culture in the target medium. The medium was refreshed every 2 days. For the following osteogenic-related studies, the P3-BMSCs were subsequently seeded in 6-well plates at a cell density of \(15\,\times\,10^{5}\) cells \(\mathrm{well}^{-1}\) using normal medium. Once BMSCs proliferation reached about \(80\%\) confluence, the target culture solutions were added to start osteogenic induction.
After culturing for 7 days, the samples were cleaned twice with PBS and fixed in \(4\%\) PFA for \(30\,\mathrm{~min~}\). The cells were then rinsed twice with PBS and stained in nitroblue tetrazolium chlorid/5-bromo-4-chloro-3-indolyl phosphate (NBT/BCIP) solution following the protocol. The morphologies of the surfaces were examined under a stereomicroscope (OLYMPUS, Japan). Alp activity was detected by an Alp activity kit following the manufacturer's instructions after culturing for 7 days. Briefly, cells were lysed by ultrasonic vibration and then incubated with substrate solution at \(37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for \(1\,\mathrm{~h~}\). The final colored production was measured at \(450\,\mathrm{~nm}\) on a microplate reader. The Alp activity was normalized to the total protein content determined by a BCA protein assay kit.
## 2.11 Collagen secretion
