## 2.12 Migration assay
The effect of the \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) on HUVECs migration was evaluated using a wound-healing migration assay in vitro. HUVECs were seeded in the 12-well plate at density of \(8\times10^{4}\) cells per well and cultured until reaching about \(90\%\) confluence. "Scars" were created by a steril \(100~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) pipet tip in the middle of the well. Then the fresh DMEM media containing different concentrations of \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) (0, 50, 100, 200, \(500\,\upmu\mathrm{g}\cdot\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\)) were added into the corresponding wells. After being incubated for \(24~\mathrm{h}\), the cells were fixed and photographed (OLYMPUS, Japan). The quantitative analysis of migration was measured according to the number of migrated cells by Image J software. To simulate the spontaneous migration of HUVECs, the \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74s}\) were placed on the lower side in full endothelial cell culture medium (ECM). At the same time, \(5\times10^{4}\) HUVECs were added to the upper chamber with serum-starved ECM in Transwell inserts (Corning, \(5~{\upmu\mathrm{m}}\) pores) referring to previous research [38]. The migration proceeded for \(8\,\mathrm{~h~}\) and those remaining cells in the upper chamber were removed, while other cells migrating to the lower side of the Transwell were fixed and successively stained with crystal violet. Observation was accomplished under a microscope (Olympus, Japan). For quantitative analysis, \(10\%\) acetic acid was added to each well to dissolve the stain for \(15~\mathrm{min}\) at RT, and the absorbance at \(560\;\mathrm{nm}\) was measured using a microplate reader.
## 2.13 Nitric oxide (NO) secretion
According to the manufacturer's instructions, the NO content of exocytosis is determined by nitrate reduction reaction (JianChen, Nanjing China). Briefly, the supernatant of the culture medium was collected via centrifugation \((10,000~\mathrm{rpm}, 30\ \mathrm{min})\) for subsequent reagent preparation, sample preparation, and assay procedures. After incubation with substrate solution at RT for \(1\ \mathrm{h}\), the color development reagent was then added to sample, and production was immediately measured at \(450\ \mathrm{nm}\) on a microplate reader. Still the concentration of NO was determined by a linear interpolation of the standard curve.
## 2.14 Reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) analysis
We investigated the expression of osteogenic-related genes in BMSCs and endothelial nitric oxide synthase (eNos) gene in HUVECs using RT-PCR. The BMSCs cells were cultured with \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\) at a cell density of \(1\times10^{5}\) cells \(\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) for 7 days. After that the cells were washed twice with PBS, and the total RNA was extracted using RNAzol reagent. Then the RNA concentrations were determined by spectrophotometry. The total RNA was reverse-transcribed into complementary DNA (cDNA) using a PrimeScript RT reagent kit. We carried out RT-PCR on \(Alp\), collagen 1 (Col1) and runtrelated transcription factor 2 (Runx2) using SYBR Premix Ex TaqII. A density of \(2\times10^{4}\) cells \(\mathrm{mL}^{-1}\) HUVECs cells were co-incubation with the medium containing \(\mathrm{m/n-Mg-MOF74}\). After 3 days, the total RNA of cells was also collected by RNAzol reagent followed reverse-transcribed into cDNA. The eNos gene were detected by using SYBR Premix Ex TaqII. The primer sequences are listed in Table 1. The relative expression levels of the target genes were normalized based on the expression levels of the reference gene \(\upbeta\)-actin. Each analysis was repeated twice.
## 2.15 Western blot analysis
To complete Western blot analysis, following the same requirements of cell culture in the RT-PCR experiment, the BMSCs cultured for 7 days and HUVECs cultured for 3 days were collected as samples, respectively. All the cells were homogenized for total protein extraction with the protein concentrations determined by the PierceTM Rapid Gold BCA Protein Assay Kit (Thermo Fisher Co., MA, USA). Equal amounts of proteins were subjected to Western blotting. The primary Abs were: anti-rat Runx2; anti-human eNos; anti-rat GAPDH and anti-human GAPDH (1:1,000 dilutions, Affinity Co). Western blotting signals were detected using a BIORAD ChemiDoc XRS chemiluminescence system (Bio-Rad Inc., CA, USA). The intensity of autoradiogram for Western blot was quantified using Image J software. The band intensity was normalized to that of the landing control.
## 2.16 Animal feeding
Male SD rats (6 weeks old with body weight around \(170\ \mathrm{g}\)) and Male Kunming (KM) mice (4 weeks old with body weight around \(30\ \mathrm{g}\)) were approved by the Institutional review committee of Sichuan University, School of Medicine and the National Institutes of Health (Chengdu, China). Rats were provided with enrichment material, chow and water ad libitum. Animal housing conditions were maintained at \(21\ ^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\), \(50\%\) humidity and a \(12\mathrm{-h/12\mathrm{-h}}\) light-dark cycle. All animals were maintained and used in accordance with the Guidelines of the Animal Ethics Committee at the Research Center for Eco-Environmental Sciences, Chinese Academy of Sciences.
